          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bheṣaja \"healing; a remedy\" is formed from bhiṣaj \"a healer, a physician\" (MW), already in the Rigveda. bhiṣaj is inherited from Indo-Iranian, with a cousin in Avestan (EtymDB)."
            }
